{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Go Context & Logging Enforcer",
  "description": "Ensures Go functions accept context.Context as first parameter and use structured logging with proper context propagation, operation timing, and error handling",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "src/api/*.go"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "When modifying or creating Go functions in this backend:\nMUST DO:\n- Accept context.Context as first parameter and pass it through all calls\n- Use context-aware logging: logInfo(ctx, msg, key, value), logError(ctx, msg, \"error\", err)\n- Log operation start/completion with relevant attributes like dataset_id, player_count, duration_ms\n- Log errors with context before returning them\n- Log cache hits/misses and performance metrics for slow operations\n\nPattern:\nfunc MyFunction(ctx context.Context, param string) error {\n    logInfo(ctx, \"Starting operation\", \"param\", param)\n    start := time.Now()\n    \n    // Your logic here\n    if err != nil {\n        logError(ctx, \"Operation failed\", \"error\", err, \"param\", param)\n        return err\n    }\n    \n    logDebug(ctx, \"Operation completed\", \"duration_ms\", time.Since(start).Milliseconds())\n    return nil\n}\n\nKey Points:\n- Always propagate context\n- Log with structured key-value pairs\n- Include operation timing for significant work\n- Don't log sensitive data or large payloads\n\nReview the modified Go code and ensure it follows these patterns. If any functions are missing context parameters or proper logging, provide specific suggestions for improvement."
  }
}